{
 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was met. Five settings on five different scenes failed in every repeat: 023b7fcc at -1.5 s (S2), 096988dd at +1.5 s (S11), 09a95ffa at -1.5 s (S14), 12855a41 at 0 s (S24) and 19f339ba at -1 s (S26). All of them used the lead car at 0.5x speed. Each 90% range is only just above 0.5, so these are confirmed as failing in most runs, not as near-certain. However, only S2 and S14 look like the policy rear-ending the slowed lead car, and even there the gap at handoff was already short, so blame is mostly unclear. The other three are different kinds of failure. At S11 the policy drifts left into a car in the next lane, even at 2 Hz. At S26 it brakes hard for no reason and a following replayed car hits it. At S24 the front contact comes 0.5 s after handoff and may be caused by the replay or the lead car's bounding box rather than the policy.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "023b7fcc with the lead shifted -1.5 s at 0.5x speed is the clearest real rear-end case. Every run closed on slow lead car 12, eased off only slightly, bent its path left at the last moment and hit the car's rear. The gap at handoff was already short, so the triage marks most of these runs 'unclear' rather than the policy's fault. The single run at -2 s also failed, but there the ego steered left out of its lane rather than rear-ending the lead.",
    "settings": [
