    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "09a95ffa at -1.5 s, 0.5x is a lead-braking failure. The policy took over with about 5 m of gap, closing at about 4 m/s, braked only lightly and hit lead vehicle 1's rear. The handoff state left very little room, so the triage marks policy fault as unclear. The neighbouring shifts -2 s and -1 s did not fail.",
    "settings": [
     "S14",
     "S13",
     "S15"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "096988dd at +1.5 s, 0.5x fails, but not by rear-ending the lead. Every run drifted left against a STRAIGHT/RIGHT route command and hit vehicle 41 in the next lane, with the policy at fault. The single run at +2 s failed the same way. Earlier shifts on this scene did not fail. Left drift is still present at 2 Hz.",
    "settings": [
     "S11",
     "S12",
     "S8",
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "19f339ba at -1 s, 0.5x is not a lead-vehicle failure. With no car close ahead, the policy braked hard for no reason (about 17 m/s down to about 5 to 6 m/s) and drifted left. Replayed vehicle 28, which cannot react, then hit it from behind and on the right side. The policy is at fault for the phantom braking, but the collision depends on non-reactive traffic.",
    "settings": [
